WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.680
Naruto is one of the most popular&nbsp;
anime franchises of all time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:10.480
With over 940 episodes in the Naruto series, and&nbsp;
multiple movies, new fans may feel overwhelmed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.080
We'll explain the correct order in which to&nbsp;
experience the sprawling Naruto franchise.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.000
"You can do this! Believe it!"

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.280
Naruto opens with mischievous Naruto&nbsp;
defacing a Mount Rushmore-esque cliff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.720
portraying the Hidden Leaf Village's elders. At&nbsp;
the time, he's a goofy troublemaker, friendless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.160
and pathetically unskilled. Unsurprisingly, he's&nbsp;
mocked by his classmates, especially his crush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:42.000
Sakura, who's in love with the ultra-cool Sasuke.&nbsp;
But soon enough, things turn around for Naruto.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.920
He becomes a shinobi, gets on a team with Sakura&nbsp;
and Sasuke taught by the impressive Kakashi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.960
rescues Sasuke from a seemingly undefeatable foe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.720
destroys all expectations in the Chunin Exams,&nbsp;
defeats a tailed beast, and takes on a legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.840
ninja as his sensei. Plus, he learns the&nbsp;
Rasengan, one of his most powerful moves.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.920
Since Team Seven is still together in the first&nbsp;
Naruto movie, Ninja Clash in the Land of Snow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.040
it must take place before Sasuke leaves in&nbsp;
Episode 108. It must also occur before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.680
mission that begins in Episode 102, which&nbsp;
results in Sasuke's injury. Furthermore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.000
Naruto has the Rasengan, so it has&nbsp;
to take place after Episode 96.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.440
As Sakura is in Episode 99 and all three are&nbsp;
together in Hidden Leaf Village in Episode 101,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.720
this would be the perfect place for&nbsp;
them to go on their snow mission.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.240
With all that in mind, this movie&nbsp;
is a whole lot of fun. It introduces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.240
some cool Hidden Leaf Village ponchos,&nbsp;
features killer snow-strewn battles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.840
unveils some of Kakashi's best jutsu, and&nbsp;
culminates in Naruto's multi-colored Rasengan.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.200
This run of Naruto episodes contains one&nbsp;
of the most compelling arcs in the series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.520
Naruto and his fellow genin — or junior&nbsp;
ninjas — set off to bring Sasuke back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.280
led by the recently promoted Shikamaru. Each&nbsp;
young shinobi fights high above his level in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.080
this storyline, which also introduces cooperation&nbsp;
with their new allies, the Three Sand Siblings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.840
Furthermore, the arc ends in Naruto's&nbsp;
first great showdown with Sasuke.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.120
In the Naruto manga, this arc is what ends young&nbsp;
Naruto's story. Most of what follows in the anime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.280
is considered filler. You could skip the next&nbsp;
60 episodes if you're only looking for canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.080
but we advise otherwise — why give up on&nbsp;
what ends up being a whole lot of fun?

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.960
This is a really unique movie because&nbsp;
it brings Naruto, Sakura, Shikamaru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.040
and Kankuro together. Also, it includes&nbsp;
heavily armed battleships and soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.120
neither of which appear in the series proper.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.200
While there aren't signposts in the filler&nbsp;
episodes that might help identify where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.160
Naruto movies fit after Sasuke's departure,&nbsp;
there are some fan theories about their order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:48.080
One says Stone of Gelel takes place after Episode&nbsp;
147 because the movie originally premiered at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.280
same time as Mizuki Strikes Back. Supporting&nbsp;
this is the fact that Naruto and Shikamaru work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.920
together during this arc — it makes sense, then,&nbsp;
that they continue that cooperation in this film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.840
Other fans maintain Stone of Gelel occurs after&nbsp;
Episode 160. Ultimately, it's up to you!
 
 

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.960
This stretch of Naruto contains more fun filler&nbsp;
episodes, though none feature any developments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.680
vital to the central story. Some viewers suggest&nbsp;
powering through the series by skipping Episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:19.280
143 through 219. But if you do so, you'll miss&nbsp;
episodes that showcase characters' deepening bonds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.160
and growing skills. If the whole point of watching&nbsp;
Naruto is to be entertained, this run delivers. 
 
 

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.080
The final movie of the original Naruto series,&nbsp;
Crescent Moon Kingdom is most notable for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.120
replacing Sasuke with Rock Lee and showing off&nbsp;
the team's new warm-weather outfits. Guardians of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:40.400
the Crescent Moon Kingdom is placed after Episode&nbsp;
196 because it was released around the same time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.840
as that episode. Plus, scenes from the movie made&nbsp;
it into the opening of Episodes 197 through 199.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.600
But again, both Naruto movies,&nbsp;
Guardians of the Crescent Moon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.920
Kingdom and Legend of the Stone of Gelel,&nbsp;
could theoretically be thrown anywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.920
as long as they end up among the many&nbsp;
filler episodes that finish the series. 
 
 

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:04.080
Naruto ends with yet more filler episodes.These&nbsp;
episodes are usually a flashback to backstory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.600
a mission with people from different teams&nbsp;
thrown together to hone their skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:13.200
a display of strengthening alliances, or an&nbsp;
exploration of a "What if?" scenario. Episode 220,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:19.120
in which Naruto leaves with the legendary sannin&nbsp;
Jiraiya, is tied to the same event in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.440
and is therefore canon. If you're looking to&nbsp;
speed through the series, jump to this episode.
 
 

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:29.280
Naruto: Shippuden opens from the point of view&nbsp;
of an unseen person, running down mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.240
corridors. We've jumped almost three years into&nbsp;
the future, from the end of the first series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:39.680
It's a bit confusing, but from the moment "Hero's&nbsp;
Come Back!!" by Japanese hip-hop group Nobodyknows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.480
starts to play over the series' first opening&nbsp;
sequence, it's impossible not to get excited.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.520
The series opens with a bang, as the Akatsuki&nbsp;
attack Hidden Sand Village, capturing Gaara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.360
decimating the Sand forces, and almost killing&nbsp;
Kankuro. Naruto is more mature, Sakura is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.000
significantly stronger, and all their young&nbsp;
friends have aged up into formidable shinobi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.400
Plus, Naruto has upgraded his blue and orange&nbsp;
outfit to a sleek black and orange look.
 
 

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.720
Unfortunately, the Naruto: Shippuden movies can&nbsp;
be even tougher to fit into the right order than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.200
the original Naruto flicks. Not only are there&nbsp;
simply more episodes and arcs to sort through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.040
some of these movies have serious&nbsp;
inconsistencies with the canon story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.840
That said, this one is relatively easy to fit.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:28.160
Naruto Shippuden the Movie premiered during the&nbsp;
Kazekage Rescue arc, which ends at Episode 32. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:34.080
this movie, we see a team made up of Naruto,&nbsp;
Sakura, Rock Lee, and Neji. Neji is the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.440
person from their class who's reached the elite&nbsp;
status of jonin. Like many other Naruto movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:44.240
grand salvation occurs in this one, thanks&nbsp;
to a special version of Naruto's Rasengan.
 
 

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:50.160
In these episodes, Team Seven is reformed&nbsp;
with Sai, an untrustworthy but powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.040
ninja from the mysterious Foundation, who becomes&nbsp;
Sasuke's permanent replacement. Captain Yamato,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:00.160
a former Anbu black ops ninja, is brought in to&nbsp;
head the team in place of an injured Kakashi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.640
In this run, we see more of the Akatsuki's&nbsp;
plans, more about Danzo's techniques,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.240
and even a reunion between Naruto&nbsp;
and the now frighteningly powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.360
Sasuke — the scene depicted in&nbsp;
the opening to this new series.
 
 

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.520
The most notable elements of Naruto Shippuden the&nbsp;
Movie: Bonds are its airships, a very advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:22.640
technology, and a Zero-Tails — neither of which&nbsp;
are ever mentioned before or after this movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.280
Since episodes 70 and 71 are non-canon,&nbsp;
you can watch this after either of those,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:32.400
before you return to canon storylines&nbsp;
at 72. What happens in this flick? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.600
Orochimaru is sick and Sasuke is still doing his&nbsp;
bidding, which brings him together with Naruto as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.640
they take on a man who may have a technique that&nbsp;
could help the ailing Orochimaru. This limits the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:48.160
film to happening before Episode 114, when Sasuke&nbsp;
and Orochimaru's relationship comes to a head.
 
 

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.680
A lot happens in this stretch of episodes.&nbsp;
Here, we witness the death of a major sensei,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.680 --> 00:07:00.560
the rise of the new Ino-Shika-Cho team, and Naruto&nbsp;
inventing a new super-powerful jutsu. Though the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:05.680
second half of this run — from Episode 91 to&nbsp;
Episode 112 — is considered quasi-canon, it does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.000
contain a tailed beast which makes some impact&nbsp;
on the storyline. You should give this a watch.
 
 

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.800
Will of Fire is one of the few movies&nbsp;
with references to things from the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.880
which make it clear that it has to take&nbsp;
place after the Kakashi Chronicles episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:25.520
which end with Episode 120. Also, Naruto, Sai, and&nbsp;
Sakura break village rules and follow Kakashi, an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:30.720
act of disobedience Sai would only have been able&nbsp;
to commit after some time spent with Team Seven.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:35.840
In Will of Fire, shinobi boasting Kekkei Genkai&nbsp;
abilities have been stolen from everywhere but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.720
Hidden Leaf Village, casting suspicion upon the&nbsp;
villagers. When Kakashi is compelled to leave the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.760
village through a mysterious curse implanted&nbsp;
in him, Tsunade allows him to go as an act of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.720
self-sacrifice. But, as previously mentioned, Team&nbsp;
Seven follows, joined by other teams in support.
 
 

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:57.680
There is a huge death in this run, one that&nbsp;
hits Naruto especially hard. The Akatsuki also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.480
seriously increase their activity, and&nbsp;
Jiraiya is haunted by a student from his past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:07.040
In an especially important flashback, Jiraiya&nbsp;
even offers the viewers a major revelation as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.000
to Naruto's parentage. Sasuke finally gets the&nbsp;
revenge that has motivated him for most of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.720
life ... and realizes he knew nothing. In the&nbsp;
aftermath, he joins the seriously-dwindled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.600
Akatsuki. This stretch of episodes contains an&nbsp;
arc some fans call filler, which actually ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.400
up having a big role in later episodes. Bottom&nbsp;
line: These episodes are impactful and important.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.000
"Oh Yeah??"
 
 

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.280
Naruto Shippuden the Movie: The Lost Tower has&nbsp;
to occur within a very small window of canon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.840
It happens after the death of a major character,&nbsp;
but before that person's killer launches a tragic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:42.960
attack. Naruto discovers this heavy death&nbsp;
in Episode 152, helps the village deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.720
the investigation in Episode 153 and Episode&nbsp;
154, and is transported to a far-off land for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:55.040
secluded training in Episode 155. So, this&nbsp;
movie has to happen between 154 and 155.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.360
The Lost Tower features an interesting&nbsp;
Naruto/Yamato time-travel element,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:03.040
in which our hero comes face-to-face with&nbsp;
the ninja the audience now understands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.840
to be his father. Moreover, the action&nbsp;
scenes and animation are amazing.
 
 

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:14.000
A powerful Akastuki member rains devastation on&nbsp;
Hidden Leaf Village while Naruto is off training.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.640
When Naruto returns, we see the troublemaker&nbsp;
whom everybody once despised finally gaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.840
the admiration, respect, and love of Hidden&nbsp;
Leaf Village. We also learn about the power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:29.520
of a new ocular jutsu known as the Rinnegan, a&nbsp;
Kekkei Genkai ability a few steps up from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.800
Byakugan and Sharingan. Meanwhile, the Akatsuki&nbsp;
lose the man we'd long believed to be their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:40.000
leader. As it turns out, the once-foolish Tobi is&nbsp;
actually much more astute than we'd ever imagined.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.440
"Yay! Naruto!"
 
 

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.000
Of all the movies in the series, this is the&nbsp;
toughest to place due to inconsistencies. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.760
Raikage still has both arms,&nbsp;
yet Naruto knows Killer Bee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.600
neither of which occur at the same time in&nbsp;
the series. Those inconsistencies aside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.120
the fact that Naruto has mastered Sage Mode and&nbsp;
knows who his father is places this movie after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.920
Pain's attack on Hidden Leaf Village. Plus, it&nbsp;
has to happen before the Five Kage Summit arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.560
which starts at Episode 197. So, we're&nbsp;
putting Blood Prison after Episode 196,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:17.600
with the caveat that this movie is so non-canon&nbsp;
it might be impossible to truly pinpoint.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.200
Blood Prison is also unique in that&nbsp;
Naruto isn't joined by any of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.400
Hidden Leaf Village friends for the&nbsp;
majority of the film. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:28.160
he has to make new allies within the&nbsp;
prison where he's wrongly incarcerated.
 
 

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.920
Though Road to Ninja: Naruto the Movie is&nbsp;
technically non-canon, it has some relevance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.920
as it's a depiction of what Tobi's&nbsp;
genjutsu world would really look like.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:43.200
In Road to Ninja, Naruto and Sakura are&nbsp;
transferred to Tobi's Infinite Tsukuyomi world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.920
where Naruto's parents are still alive and&nbsp;
Sakura's parents died defending the village.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.880
Naruto already met his mom in Episode 246, so&nbsp;
his ability to identify her in the movie places&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:59.200
it after the end of that arc in Episode 251.&nbsp;
Episode 252 begins the run-up to the Shinobi War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:04.640
with Tobi too busy trying to attain Nagato's&nbsp;
Rinnegan to cast the Infinite Tsukuyomi. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.080
this movie has to happen between&nbsp;
Episodes 251 and 252.
 
 
 
 

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:15.920
This massive run of 240 episodes is impossible&nbsp;
to properly describe in a timely fashion. Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:19.760
we encounter the Fourth Great Shinobi&nbsp;
War, Naruto and Sasuke's final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:24.800
and Naruto's ascendancy to a status unimaginable&nbsp;
to anybody who knew the boy growing up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:29.360
These episodes feature amazing battle after&nbsp;
amazing battle, creating an absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.240
jaw-dropping storyline that goes toe-to-toe with&nbsp;
the greatest anime sagas around. Though again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:39.600
Episode 311 should be watched immediately&nbsp;
after 251, not in its series order.
 
 

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.309
The Last: Naruto the Movie is the only canon&nbsp;
Naruto movie. It sets in motion so much that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.309 --> 00:11:45.359
impacts the lives of the characters that it is&nbsp;
absolutely a required watch. This movie takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:50.320
place after the Great Shinobi War and Naruto's&nbsp;
showdown with Sasuke, but before the final arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:56.160
that takes place from Episode 494 through Episode&nbsp;
500. This movie also jumps forward a couple years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:01.360
bringing Naruto into young manhood. So,&nbsp;
between Episodes 493 and 494 it is.
 
 

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:07.520
This run of episodes closes out Shippuden. It's&nbsp;
a couple years after the Great Shinobi War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.560
and there are lots of good feelings going around.&nbsp;
It's been a long journey — 720 episodes and 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:17.440
movies long, to be precise — and the troubled,&nbsp;
no-good boy ninja with a demon inside him has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:21.520
become the greatest shinobi in the land.&nbsp;
These episodes benefit from that fact.
 
 

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:28.640
Naruto's story doesn't end there — he and his&nbsp;
wife Hinata have a son named Boruto. As with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:34.720
original series, Boruto: Naruto Next Generations&nbsp;
is based on a manga created by Masashi Kishimoto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:38.480
which follows a new boy ninja growing up&nbsp;
in the shadow of his father's greatness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:42.720
Episodes 1 through 49 chronicle Boruto's&nbsp;
life as he makes his way in the academy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.600
and his early days on Team Konohamaru.&nbsp;
Though Naruto was a horrible student and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:52.000
a social pariah in his early days, Boruto's&nbsp;
journey is very different from his father's.
 
 

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:58.800
In this movie, Boruto has graduated from the&nbsp;
academy and joined Team Konohamaru with Sarada&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:03.040
and Mitsuki. The story told here is also&nbsp;
explored in the series, so if you prefer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:08.000
you can watch Episodes 50 through 65 and check&nbsp;
out the movie after, or skip the movie entirely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.480
The movie was released before the series, and&nbsp;
is an adaptation of the Boruto manga, making it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:17.120
canon. Take note: There are some details of the&nbsp;
story that differ between movies and series.
 
 

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:24.400
Boruto's path to becoming a great shinobi is&nbsp;
certainly different from his father's, but taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.640
it in is just as fun and memorable. The show&nbsp;
is still running, and, given the length of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:33.680
previous series, that might remain the case for a&nbsp;
very long time. For however long this saga remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.960
ongoing, devoted fans will flock to it, eager to&nbsp;
enjoy the adventures of these powerful fighters.

